Source of debt
If the taxpayer does not understand why they have a debt, a discussion about the possible cause may assist them to understand their circumstances and enable better tax planning decisions to avoid a future tax bill shock.

Use Account explanationOpens in a new window to help the taxpayer find out why they have a debt.

ATO processed known amounts
The taxpayer may have received a letter as part of the Lodgment Reminder Strategy (LRS) pilot. Further information about the LRS pilot is available on the Activity Statement - Lodgment Reminder Strategy.Opens in a new window If the taxpayer does not lodge their activity statement by the due date in the letter, we add the amounts we have on record to their Integrated Taxpayer Account (ICA), this is known internally as Processed known amounts (PKA).

PKA are amounts recorded from STP reporting that will pre-fill into an activity statement with status Dispatched (DSP) in IPS.

PKA will:

pre-fill the activity statement and appear as a debt on the taxpayer's ICA
also process amounts for PAYGI amount option and GST instalments (GSTI) if applicable.
PKA can only apply to employers lodging via STP starting from 1 September 2023. Large PAYGW withholders are not part of the LRS and will not receive PKA treatment.

