Excess Transfer Balance Tax
The Transfer Balance Cap (TBC) is the limit on the amount of superannuation savings a taxpayer can have in 'tax-free' retirement income stream accounts.

If the taxpayer exceeds their TBC, we will send them an Excess Transfer Balance (ETB) determination.

If the taxpayer has received an excess transfer balance determination, they will receive an assessment for Excess Transfer Balance Tax (ETBT).

The ETBT is calculated:

on the notional earnings from the day they exceeded the TBC

to the end of the day they fully commute their excess (excess transfer balance period).

ETBT is due and payable 21 days after the assessment or amended assessment is served to the taxpayer. General Interest Charge (GIC) will accrue if any amount remains unpaid after the due date.

When the ETBT is overdue, the amount should be included in your whole of taxpayer payment negotiation. The taxpayer can enter a payment plan to pay this debt.

