ECP profiling - Know your taxpayer
A red flag would be identified and financials to be requested in the following example.

Wealth Summary (Total Net Assets) = Negative Asset position of -$90,013.00.
The Companies Total assets was worth $1,385,481.00. It has an outstanding tax debt owing of $1,475,494.00.
Therefore the taxpayer has no working capital to refinance or borrow against. This is because it is in the red for amount of -$90,013.00.
Requesting financial information
Use this information if you determine ;you need to request financial information to make a decision.

Request the following information:

a proposal to pay for all amounts owed to the ATO in the shortest possible timeframe, while allowing for all future tax obligations to be met by the due date
details of events and contributing factors which has caused the debt to accrue
steps taken to mitigate the debt (such as, changes in operations)
any other additional information that may assist the ATO in assessing their proposal
the most recent statement for each financial institution account held (for 6 months)
the following documents for the current financial year to date and the previous 2 financial years
detailed balance sheet or statement of financial position
detailed profit and loss statement or statement of financial performance
details of any overdraft or loan facilities - including term loans and bank bill facilities, hire purchases and leasing agreements what funds are still available to be able to be drawn upon? how much is currently owing? how much are the monthly repayments? what is the limit of the overdraft facility?
list of aged creditors (30/60/90 days)
list of aged debtors (30/60/90 days)
projected cash flow statements for the term of the payment plan.
