Self Help
ATO website
Success alert:Help the caller go to the page while on the phone.
This is a chance to educate the caller about self-help options, which may lead to:

the taxpayer using self-service in the future, and
a better taxpayer experience.
Taxpayers can obtain more information from the ATO website on:

How to payOpens in a new window and selecting the appropriate option. The latest credit card fee rates will be displayed when they use the online service

Create a myGov account and link it to the ATOOpens in a new window

by calling the Government EasyPay self-help telephony service on 1300 898 089.
Information alert:Use our self-service any time - it's easy, free and fast. Refer to Self-help services.Opens in a new window

Procedure Steps
Establish PORO
If you need to discuss the account or process payments:

establish PORO,Opens in a new window or

for GST Limited Registration Entities (LRE), go to Simplified GST ARN PORO.Opens in a new window

Payment processing times
Note: Payments,

need to reach us on or before the due date
may take up to 4 business days to be received by us and to appear on a taxpayer's ATO account
made on a weekend, Australian national public holiday or after the processing cut off time on business days will be processed on the next business day.
Information on card payment
Advise the taxpayer:

Visa, MasterCard and American Express cards are accepted

card payment fees apply, refer to Card terms and conditionsOpens in a new window on the ATO website for details. The fee payable and percentage will be advised prior to confirming payment

payments amounts must be a minimum of $1 and maximum of $20,000,000

this is not a direct debit plan. They will need to pay subsequent payments manually or set up direct debit with a bank account

the ATO does not store card details. Call recording is stopped to ensure card details are not stored.

If the taxpayer requires information on claiming a deduction for a card payment fee, go to 'Credit card payment fees' in Other deductions.Opens in a new window

Inbound correspondence contains card details
Information alert:Under no circumstances should credit/debit card details be provided in writing. Card details can only be provided verbally or by using ATO online services.
Where a document attached to a Siebel activity contains card details, complete the taxpayer's request and then escalateOpens in a new window to your coach/manager to have the card details blacked out.

If unavailable, complete a non-phone escalationOpens in a new window and update the priority to 'ASAP'.

Obtain PRN
Where the taxpayer cannot provide their Payment reference number (PRN) over the phone, for:

GST at settlement, go to Locate GST at settlement payment reference numberOpens in a new window

other accounts, go to view PRN in ICP.Opens in a new window

ICP one-off payments
Complete the steps in the following table to process a card payment in ICP.

Step	Action
1

Open ICP and select:

One-off payments from the Client menu

Account type and account sequence number from the drop-down the taxpayer wants to make a payment

Role from the drop-down if required.

Determine if the taxpayer has multiple accounts of the same type. For example, multiple ITA's. If:

yes, match the applicable account to the balance owing that will display on the selecting account

no, continue with procedure

Information
ATO Staff are unable to process payments to accounts with a $0.00 balance on the taxpayer’s behalf.

If ICP is unavailable, advise the taxpayer of alternative payment options available for paying the ATO.

2

Confirm the Amount to pay with the taxpayer.

3

Manually pause the recording to prevent collection of sensitive information as below:

right-click the AIMOpens in a new window icon

select

Pause Monitoring, and

Stop button in the Voice Authentication (VA) dashboard in the Communication toolbar.

Advise the taxpayer call monitoring has stopped to ensure card details are not recorded.

If the call recording cannot be paused:

end the call

enter break code '9'

call the taxpayer back using your desktop phone (not the toolbar).

Notify your manager so your adherence file can be adjusted.

4

Go to ICP and select Payment methods from the Client menu.

Check if there are stored credit card details in ICP. If the taxpayer:

has a stored credit card on their account,

confirm the last 4 digits of the stored credit card with the taxpayer

check the Card Unusable Indicator. If it is

Y, the card cannot be used as it has expired. Select NEW CARD and go to step 5
N, the card is still usable, and the taxpayer can use it for the payment. If the card on file is correct, go to step 6
does not have a stored credit card or does not want to use a stored credit card, go to step 5.

5


Enter the credit card details provided by the taxpayer. Complete the following fields:

Cardholder name

Card number

Card verification code

Expiry date

Contact details (phone number or email)

Billing address.

Note: The contact details and billing address should be the details that the taxpayer has provided to their financial institution. If they are using a pre-paid debit card that is not registered, they should use the details they have provided to the ATO or contact the card issuer for advice about which details to use.

Ask the taxpayer if they would like to store the credit card details for future payments. Advise the taxpayer:

the ATO does not 'store' a taxpayer's card details

cards will show on systems in a 'masked' format (for example, 12345*****6789)

the ATO uses Worldline Australia to store card details on their behalf. Worldline Australia is the Reserve Bank of Australia's (RBA) payment gateway service provider. This ensures our systems are secure.

Select:

the radio button according to their response

Authorise.

6


Advise the taxpayer the:

payment amount

fee amount

transaction total.

If the taxpayer is happy to proceed, select Submit.

If the transaction was:

successful,

a confirmation page will display and includes the receipt number for both the principle and fee payments

not successful, then

confirm the credit card details with the taxpayer. If the credit card details were

correct, advise them to check their credit card account or try another card

not correct, return to step 5 and process the payment again with the correct details.

7

Manually resume recording as follows:

right-click the AIM button

select

Resume Monitoring, and

Start button in the VA dashboard in the Communication toolbar to enable voice authentication.

8

Add a noteOpens in a new window using the Card payment template in the Notes fly-out tab.

This is the end of the procedure.

